. That is 18× weaker than Earth’s gravity, so the clip most likely plays about 4.3× slower than real life.","comparisons":[{"param":"g","measured":0.5418876867463923,"sigma":0.011421810146178652,"reference":9.80665,"label":"standard gravity on Earth","errorPct":-94.47428340211599,"withinSigma":811.1465866339304}],"eyeball":{"confidence":"low-medium: L ~1 m estimated from tennis-ball scale vs stand height, T ~1.6 s estimated from swing timing; consistent with standard g, not a precise measurement","estimates":[{"quantity":"g","unit":"m/s^2","value":9.8}],"law_in_words":"Small-angle simple pendulum period is T = 2*pi*sqrt(L/g) so g = 4*pi^2*L/T^2. Here the string swings with full length L from top pivot on the right and shortened length from the middle peg/clamp on the left, so full period is half long period plus half short period: T = pi*sqrt(L_long/g) + pi*sqrt(L_short/g). Equal max heights on the dashed line show energy conservation. Using apparent L_long ~1.0 m and observed interrupted period ~1.6-1.7 s gives g ~9.8.","model":"muse-spark-1.3"},"whatIf":[{"label":"if gravity were Earth-like","param":"g","factor":18.1,"px":[{"x":1026.8725236256596,"y":479.10056448636476},{"x":1023.8288562369321,"y":482.0019711399321},{"x":1016.5912299544083,"y":488.6491767415119},{"x":1004.9918308936853,"y":498.61222655958755},{"x":988.8244069488585,"y":511.2189218473599},{"x":967.9163483999582,"y":525.5710226508659},{"x":942.2150976244404,"y":540.5812086667994},{"x":911.8754491221389,"y":555.0387299559013},{"x":877.3301867463707,"y":567.7064457715244},{"x":839.3253829865159,"y":577.4432445947821},{"x":798.9057348109101,"y":583.3358294816057},{"x":757.3451774739538,"y":584.8162212960642},{"x":716.0316969891736,"y":581.7399193741253},{"x":676.3282724658143,"y":574.4063879170675},{"x":639.439110604803,"y":563.5168686419956},{"x":606.3087072747315,"y":550.0797293858657},{"x":577.571490791387,"y":535.2849674480728},{"x":553.5559489890522,"y":520.373323993178},{"x":534.3344003250071,"y"